window.products.push({"id":324520,"name":"Ceramic Stovetop Cookware, 2-Quart Stockpot/Casserole in Eggplant Purple by Robin Shea Pareto Stone","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71xEqTnZvXL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Pareto Stone by Robin Shea \"80% Healthy, 20% Indulgent, and 100% Delicious!\", is Robin Shea's mantra. It is a lifestyle designed to help you be thoughtful about what you eat without sacrificing life's greatest pleasure: good food. The Pareto Stone collection embodies her vision by featuring three ceramic cooking vessels with a nonporous, all-natural glaze. They make cooking nutritious foods more convenient because the cookware can move straight from the refrigerator to the microwave or oven -- which is essential to consistently making healthy dinners for a busy family. Also, the clean-up is a snap! You can wash by hand or place the cookware in the dishwasher. What truly sets Pareto Stone apart is the advanced thermal shock resistance. The all-ceramic cooking vessel can handle sweeping temperature changes without cracking. This means you can use these wonderful pots on the stove, in the oven, on the grill, and so much more. You will not find stoneware casserole dishes like these anywhere else! Features: Bonus Recipe Card includes some of Robin's favorites. Bonus Recipe Card includes some of Robin's favorites. Borosilicate Glass Lid is highly heat resistant and safe to use in the oven. Borosilicate Glass Lid is highly heat resistant and safe to use in the oven. Healthy Ceramic Stoneware is non-toxic and non-reactive. Healthy Ceramic Stoneware is non-toxic and non-reactive. Serve In Style when you take these beautiful casserole dishes straight from the oven to your dinner table. Serve In Style when you take these beautiful casserole dishes straight from the oven to your dinner table. About Robin Robin Shea is leading the way in the healthy food movement. She is best known for her “80/20 Healthy Living” approach. This means you should eat quality, nutritious food 80% of the time, and leave yourself a little room for guilt-free indulgence 20% of the time. Mastering this approach will bring balance into your life, help you manage your weight, and keep your family healthy. Notable chefs, including Paula Deen, have championed Robin and her message. You can learn more at Robin Shea's website.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71xEqTnZvXL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Robin Shea","source_asin":"B08FFVQDDF","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-324520","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08FFVQDDF","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B08FFVQDDF","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
